        "kind": "pull_request",
        "title": "Menu bar: show reset time when quota runs out",
        "body": "Closes #2028\n\n## Summary\nAdds an opt-in Display setting — **Show reset time when quota runs out** — for the brand-icon menu bar text. In Percent, Pace, and Both modes, once the selected quota hits 0% remaining the dead value (`0%`, `0% · +60%`) is replaced with the time until reset (`↻ 2h 14m`), flipping back automatically after the reset. The combined session/weekly text (Codex/Claude) replaces only the exhausted lane (`5h ↻ 2h 15m · W 45%`).\n\nDesigned as an orthogonal toggle rather than a fifth display mode so it composes with Percent/Pace/Both and inherits the existing used/remaining and countdown/clock preferences. Default off — behavior is unchanged unless enabled.\n\n## Details\n- Exhaustion triggers on `remainingPercent <= 0` regardless of the used/remaining display setting.\n- Reuses the existing reset-time rendering incl. the `resetsAt`-missing fallbacks (trusted `resetDescription` phrases, else keep showing percent).\n- Reset time display mode and all balance/credits provider overrides are untouched; the toggle is disabled in the UI when the display mode is already Reset time.\n- The minute-tick menu bar refresh now also runs while the toggle is active and a quota is exhausted, so the countdown stays live.\n- New strings localized for all 23 locales.\n\n## Testing\n- `make test` (full sharded suite) — passed\n- `make check` (swiftformat + swiftlint) — clean\n- New unit tests: smart replacement per mode, countdown/clock styles, non-exhausted and disabled regression cases, no-metadata fallback, reset-time-mode unaffected, combined-lane replacement\n\n🤖 Generated with [Claude Code](https://claude.com/claude-code)\n",
        "branch": "feat/menu-bar-smart-reset",
